Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cranes Refuse the Postmark
- Story & Context: When the relief supply boat failed to break through the harbor pack ice in the winter of 1983, Henrik Holst broke open a dead telegraph operator's locked sea chest at the Vardø spit and found a bundle of seventy unsent aerograms tied with tarred string. Setting his LinnDrum to a swinging 102 BPM to counter the shrieking gale outside, he held a carbon microphone against a brass music box cylinder to broadcast the letters' dates across the emergency marine band. An outbound cod trawler captain was moved to tears by the unannounced transmission, later telling maritime authorities he steered by the radio melody when his compass froze, forever capturing the keeper's sung lament: "The ink gave up before the winter did."
