Track 2: Did You Sign Before the Ice Closed?
- Story & Context: Recorded inside the spiraling granite stairwell of the Slettnes light tower, Maren Lind fed a five-year-late postcard from Tromsø directly through a hole-punch mechanism to create a bespoke perforated music-box ribbon. The resulting melody was mathematically irregular and painfully sweet, played against a sparse Roland SH-101 bassline while the rhythmic clack of the lighthouse rotation mechanism leaked into every vocal track. The broadcast became an accidental public confession when amateur radio listeners in northern Scotland intercepted her faltering alto vocals, which swelled into an infectious dance chorus driven by the wounded line, "You stamped the date my heart forgot to beat."
