Track 3: Dead Letter Wow & Flutter
- Story & Context: In May 1986, long after the Vardø spit had been automated and abandoned by its human keepers, fishermen docking in Hammerfest reported that their maritime radios were still picking up an unspooling loop of music-box chimes and gated drums at 3:00 AM. Port officials who climbed the salt-encrusted tower found no squatters, only a solar-charged cassette deck and a wind-up clockwork mechanism wired to a timer, steadily playing through decaying magnetic tape. The phantom reel had worn thin and warbled in pitch, broadcasting a final, bittersweet hit of pop nostalgia to empty waters while an automated vocal loop repeated, "We sailed on promises the postman kept."
